  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Twin Prime Conjecture}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "Conjecture:\nthen:\n. forAll: N is \\integer\n  then:\n  . exists: p, q is \\integer\n    suchThat:\n    . N \\:integer.less?:/ p\n    . p is? \\(prime)::integer\n    . q = p \\.integer.+./ \\integer.two\n    . q is? \\(prime)::integer\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Twin Prime Conjecture\"\n. description: \"Above every integer bound there is a prime $p$ for which $p+2$\n                is also prime. This unboundedness formulation is equivalent to\n                the existence of infinitely many twin-prime pairs.\"\nId: \"565f765c-47cd-427f-a5b5-44c87d1a9794\"",
